{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"00b319d7ae838cc3d3bba24368ea64c217cac19ea4aca8fe59d45eca2dc63c2f","digest":{"component_or_area":"ticket close path / compaction","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py","src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","src/rebar/_store/lock.py","_compact_on_close","_compact_locked","write_lock_is_busy","ticket-write.lock.d","docs/concurrency.md","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_does_not_compact_barbet.py"],"problem_keywords":["lock contention","write lock hold","compaction performance","ticket close","store lock"],"propositions":["Closing a ticket invokes _compact_on_close which holds the store write lock continuously for minutes (measured 13m53s in production), blocking all concurrent agent writes","The compact_txn._compact_locked fold acquires a single store write lock and never releases it during the entire fold operation, including git add/commit","Removing _compact_on_close from the close path restores lock-hold time to seconds and is safe because compaction is optional housekeeping, not a correctness requirement","Compaction itself remains available via explicit rebar compact <id> command and will be re-triggered out-of-band by a scheduled sweep in a follow-up change"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787462636359167001,"uuid":"f07a0915-b085-4f78-9ca0-a4a705fdcdba"}